hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"24429","Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Ma'bad ibn Ka'b ibn Malik, from his mother, and she had prayed both qiblahs with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbidding dates and raisins to be steeped together. He said: Steep each one of them separately."
"24430","Ibrahim ibn Khalid narrated to us, Rabah narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Ka'b ibn Malik, from his mother, that Umm Mubashshir entered upon the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, during his illness in which he died, and said: By my father and mother, O Messenger of Allah, what do you suspect yourself to suffer from? For I suspect nothing but the food that he ate with you at Khaybar, and her son had died before the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: And I suspect nothing else. This is the time my aorta is being cut."
